# Multicultural Mathematics and Alternative Algorithms.

**Authors:** Philipp, Randolph A.

## Abstract
Encourages teachers to allow opportunities for students to present alternative algorithms, whether the students invent them or learn them, then lead a discussion about the meaning of the operations with the goal of students understanding why the algorithm works. Teachers with students of similar racial and ethnic backgrounds should encourage the invented algorithms their students might create. (AIM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ541751

